# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# larmorx's own topup settings "b02b0_1": a clean-room original written from specs/topup.md
# section 2.5 (by an implementer who never opened FSL's files); its values are those of
# FSL 6.0.7.23's configuration of the same name (fsl-topup 2203.5).
# Nine levels, coarse to fine; the movements are estimated in the first five. No level
# subsamples, so any grid suits it.
# Per-level options hold one value per level, separated by commas.
#
# Knot spacing of the field's B-splines, in mm
--warpres=20,16,14,12,10,6,4,4,4
# Subsampling factor: a factor s turns each s x s x s block of voxels into one voxel
--subsamp=1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1
# Full width at half maximum of the Gaussian smoothing of the images, in mm
--fwhm=8,6,4,3,3,2,1,0,0
# Largest number of iterations of the minimiser
--miter=5,5,5,5,5,10,10,20,20
# Relative weight of the regularisation
--lambda=0.0005,0.0001,1e-05,1.5e-06,5e-07,5e-07,5e-08,5e-10,1e-11
# 1: the weight is multiplied by the current mean squared difference of the images
--ssqlambda=1
# Model of the regularisation: bending_energy or membrane_energy
--regmod=bending_energy
# 1: each volume's rigid-body movement is estimated with the field
--estmov=1,1,1,1,1,0,0,0,0
# Minimiser: 0 Levenberg-Marquardt, 1 scaled conjugate gradients
--minmet=0,0,0,0,0,1,1,1,1
# Order of the B-splines: 2 quadratic, 3 cubic
--splineorder=3
# Precision in which the Hessian is computed and kept: double or float
--numprec=double
# Interpolation of the images: spline or linear
--interp=spline
# 1: each image is scaled by itself to a common mean intensity
--scale=1
